<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28082" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Marpessus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Marpēsus</span></b> , i,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μάρπησσος</span> (another
		form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μάρμησσος</span> v. Marmessus),
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in the
				Troas, on Mount Ida, home of the Erythrean Sibyl</i>, Varr. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Lact. 1, 6,
			12</span></i>.—Hence, adj.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Marpessĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ēsius</span></b> ), a,
			um, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
				Marpessus in the Troas, Marpessian</i>, <i><span class="en">Tib. 2, 5,
				67</span></i> Drisen.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
